Subject: coders/jpeg.c: only include <setjmp.h> when the JPEG delegate is built

wasm32 clang errors out on <setjmp.h> unless -mllvm -wasm-enable-sjlj is given
(the Exception-handling proposal).  coders/jpeg.c includes it one line ABOVE
the `#if defined(MAGICKCORE_JPEG_DELEGATE)` guard, so the file cannot compile
even in its delegate-free form (which is just RegisterJPEGImage /
UnregisterJPEGImage).  Move the include inside the guard.

We keep the delegate-free jpeg.c so "JPEG" still shows up in
MagickQueryFormats() and produces a proper "no decode delegate" exception
rather than "no such format".

--- a/coders/jpeg.c
+++ b/coders/jpeg.c
@@ -88,8 +88,8 @@
 #include "MagickCore/xml-tree.h"
 #include "MagickCore/xml-tree-private.h"
 #include "coders/coders-private.h"
-#include <setjmp.h>
 #if defined(MAGICKCORE_JPEG_DELEGATE)
+#include <setjmp.h>
 #define JPEG_INTERNAL_OPTIONS
 #if defined(__MINGW32__)
 # define XMD_H 1  /* Avoid conflicting typedef for INT32 */
